<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n71121" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νοῦμμος</span></b> , ὁ, Western 
			Dor.
		
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νόμος</span>
			, <i>current coin,</i> esp. of the Tarentine stater, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				590
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίτρα</span>
			, the silver equivalent of the bronze pound, ib.<i><span class="en">
				589
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			= Lat. <i>nummus</i> (sc. <i>sestertius</i>), <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Sull.</u>
				1
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>